From 3eb72e7a8b44efe2245f86e7c59df45150831cfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qualcomm-toolbox <169756160+qcom-toolbox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:40:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] umi-0170-fb-gpu-hold-workloop-console

In sweet_fb_gpu_begin(), set the hold and clean the boot framebuffer from
the CPU cache inside the framebuffer workloop's gate (fWorkLoop->runAction),
so no AppleCLCD::present() frame copy runs at the same time; mute the kernel
text console for the hold (sweet_console_muted, old value put back when the
hold ends in vsyncFired, also when it ends with the display off); skip the
power-off fade (and the copy-over that precedes it) while the hold lasts.
In the 0169 boot the console wrote an opaque black pixel over the GPU's
green band before iOS's first frame muted it, so step 22's check failed and
step 23 never ran.

Also stamp the hold-related GPU (printf) and FB (IOLog) lines with
mach_absolute_time() so their order can be read from the persistent log.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 bsd/dev/sweet_adreno.c                |  39 ++++-----
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp | 109 ++++++++++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 116 insertions(+), 32 deletions(-)

